<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recent progress in advanced reasoning and coding models is largely driven by reinforcement learning (RL) post-training, where a pre-trained base model is further improved through interaction with math, programming, or software engineering problems. It is well documented that this interactive training paradigm leads to significant improvements in model capabilities and state-of-the-art performance. Correspondingly, a rapidly growing body of work has proposed algorithmic and data-centric interventions to the reinforcement learning pipeline, with promising experimental results on academic and industry benchmarks.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Despite this progress, much of the recent research focuses on improving the RL recipe through interventions. By contrast, comparatively little is understood about the mechanisms by which RL improves the capabilities of the base model. Thus, we ask two central questions:</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<blockquote id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="S1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Through what mechanisms does RL lead to improved model capabilities?
<br class="ltx_break">What is the role of data in enabling these mechanisms?</span></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We answer these questions via a mechanistic study of RL post-training, focusing on math reasoning. Our experiments reveal two core mechanisms: <span id="S1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">strategy selection</span> which routes problems to existing reasoning patterns learned during pre-training and <span id="S1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">strategy improvement</span> which improves existing reasoning patterns. We also find that whether these mechanisms activate during training depends strongly on both the pre-training and reinforcement learning datasets. Notably, strategy selection—the largest driver of performance in our experiments—requires that the pre-training data contains reasoning patterns to select among; we do not observe novel patterns emerging through reinforcement learning.
Meanwhile, strategy improvement requires that the RL dataset consists of more difficult questions than those seen during SFT; RL training with similar problem difficulty does not improve OOD generalization.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Our experimental setup also elicits two previously-observed phenomena, <span id="S1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">strategy amplification</span>, where particular reasoning patterns appear more frequently after RL, and <span id="S1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">strategy composition</span>, where, through RL training, the model improves its ability to chain together multiple complex reasoning steps. However, we find that strategy amplification is an observable effect of strategy selection, and strategy composition is a particular instance of strategy improvement. Thus, we do not view these as separate mechanisms but rather as phenomena that can emerge from the core mechanisms of selection and improvement.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Our findings offer a new perspective into the behavior of RL post-training. We find that RL in the language model setting largely operates by refining reasoning patterns acquired during pre-training. Such refinements can significantly improve performance, but do not induce entirely new behaviors. Thus, our results emphasize the role of high-quality pre-training data as an essential component in scaling reinforcement learning. We hope our findings inspire a more holistic approach to model training and provide a mechanistic foundation for future advances in RL post-training.</p>
</div>
<section id="S1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.1 </span>Related Work</h3>

<div id="S1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Reinforcement learning is now a central component in modern language model training pipelines, and a growing body of work studies its behavior, identifying recurring phenomena such as policy sharpening <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yue et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, entropy reduction, dependence on the pre-trained model, and sensitivity to reward and data designs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">DeepSeek-AI, 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>. Our results build on this line of work by introducing a clear taxonomy of mechanisms, and a single experimental setup that manifests several mechanisms, unifying and clarifying prior observations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Among the specific mechanisms identified in our work, strategy selection was observed to some extent in prior work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tsilivis et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Matsutani et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. In contrast with these works, our findings go beyond convergence to a single strategy: we find that RL can <span id="S1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">route</span> problems to different strategies observed in the pretraining data, thereby emphasizing the role of <span id="S1.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">data diversity</span> in pretraining.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Strategy amplification has been prominently observed through the emergence of backtracking in DeepSeek-R1 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">DeepSeek-AI, 2025</a>)</cite>, and has been studied through the lens of distributional sharpening <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yue et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. Complementary analyses show that amplification can occur through entropy reduction <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cui et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, high-entropy branching tokens <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, and implicit biases in trajectory ranking <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. Distributional amplification can emerge even under spurious rewards, which triggers amplification of pretraining behaviors <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. Our experiments associate amplification with selection, offering a mechanistic explanation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Regarding strategy improvement and composition, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yuan et al., 2025</a>)</cite> demonstrate extrapolative generalization and composition in controlled settings that are closely related to strategy improvement. We observe similar findings and further show that strategy improvement can sometimes be a secondary driver of RL performance relative to strategy selection.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We survey and discuss other work related to these aspects in <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Extended Related Work ‣ Select and Improve: Understanding the Mechanics of Post-Training for Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Setup</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider a standard language model post-training setup involving both supervised fine-tuning (SFT) and reinforcement learning (RL). We adopt the following reinforcement learning notation: prompts <math id="S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> and responses <math id="S2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math> belong to prompt and response spaces <math id="S2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X},\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X},\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively and a language model <math id="S2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:\mathcal{X}\to\Delta(\mathcal{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:\mathcal{X}\to\Delta(\mathcal{Y})</annotation></semantics></math> associates a distribution over responses to any prompt. Supervised fine-tuning takes a dataset <math id="S2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{SFT}}:=\{(x_{i},y_{i})_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>SFT</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{SFT}}:=\{(x_{i},y_{i})_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> of prompt-response pairs and maximizes<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
          Our experiments operate in a chain-of-thought setting where both prompts and responses are sequence of tokens. <a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2 Setup ‣ Select and Improve: Understanding the Mechanics of Post-Training for Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> corresponds to standard token-level cross entropy loss minimization in this case.</span></span></span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{SFT}}(\pi;D_{\mathrm{SFT}}):=\sum_{(x,y)\in D_{\mathrm{SFT}}}\log\pi(y\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>SFT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>SFT</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>SFT</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{SFT}}(\pi;D_{\mathrm{SFT}}):=\sum_{(x,y)\in D_{\mathrm{SFT}}}\log\pi(y\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">using gradient-based optimization, initialized from a pre-trained language model <math id="S2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{base}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>base</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{base}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In RL, we have a dataset <math id="S2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{RL}}:=\{(x_{i})_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>RL</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{RL}}:=\{(x_{i})_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> of prompts and a reward function <math id="S2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R:\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}\to\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R:\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}\to\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> determining correctness (or quality) of response <math id="S2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> to prompt <math id="S2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. Using these, we seek to maximize</p>
<table id="S2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{RL}}(\pi;D_{\mathrm{RL}}):=\sum_{x\in D_{\mathrm{RL}}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot\mid{}x)}[R(x,y)]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>RL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>RL</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>RL</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{RL}}(\pi;D_{\mathrm{RL}}):=\sum_{x\in D_{\mathrm{RL}}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot\mid{}x)}[R(x,y)],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">again using gradient-based optimization, initialized now from the policy <math id="S2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{SFT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>SFT</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{SFT}}</annotation></semantics></math> obtained from the SFT stage. Models are primarily evaluated via the reinforcement learning objective <a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2 Setup ‣ Select and Improve: Understanding the Mechanics of Post-Training for Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> on a held out dataset of prompts <math id="S2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{val}}:=\{(x_{i})_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>val</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{val}}:=\{(x_{i})_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1 </span>Experimental setup: Finite-field arithmetic task</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout our experiments, we focus on a synthetic finite-field arithmetic task, which captures a surprising depth of behaviors through subtle changes to the basic version of the task and the training setup. Following the protocol above, we always SFT a base model (<span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct</span>) on some SFT dataset, and continue training via RL on some RL dataset, which may be from a different distribution. First we describe the task.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Prompts</h5>

<div id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Towards building a mechanistic understanding, it is essential to carefully control the set of reasoning strategies available to the model before RL training. At the same time, we want to operate at a reasonable scale so must rely on open source pre-trained models. To break away from the math reasoning ability contained within such pre-trained base models, we construct a finite-field arithmetic task where integers are replaced by abstract symbols, and the goal is to manipulate them to compute the answer. The problem begins with a randomly generated permutation to define the elements of the finite field. The subsequent computational problem takes one of two forms: evaluation or inversion (see <a href="#S2.F1" title="In Prompts ‣ 2.1 Experimental setup: Finite-field arithmetic task ‣ 2 Setup ‣ Select and Improve: Understanding the Mechanics of Post-Training for Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</p>
<ul id="S2.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.25em;">
<li id="S2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evaluation problems.</span> Evaluation problems are those where the model is given a sequence of arithmetic operations, and is tasked with performing them in order.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inversion problems.</span> Inversion problems, on the other hand, correspond to solving for an unknown variable. The model is given an unknown input <math id="S2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, and a sequence of arithmetic operations which manipulate <math id="S2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> in various ways resulting in a numerical value. The model must solve for the value of <math id="S2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="S2.F1.3" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:170.8pt;">
            
<div id="S2.F1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.F1.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="238.86" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 236.3 238.86" width="236.3"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,238.86) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 6.37 L 0 232.5 C 0 236.01 2.85 238.86 6.37 238.86 L 229.93 238.86 C 233.45 238.86 236.3 236.01 236.3 232.5 L 236.3 6.37 C 236.3 2.85 233.45 0 229.93 0 L 6.37 0 C 2.85 0 0 2.85 0 6.37 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 6.37 L 0.83 200.96 L 235.47 200.96 L 235.47 6.37 C 235.47 3.31 232.99 0.83 229.93 0.83 L 6.37 0.83 C 3.31 0.83 0.83 3.31 0.83 6.37 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 201.79 L 0.83 232.5 C 0.83 235.55 3.31 238.03 6.37 238.03 L 229.93 238.03 C 232.99 238.03 235.47 235.55 235.47 232.5 L 235.47 201.79 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.07 225.45)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:14.26em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:1.43em;font-size:10pt;" height="28.37" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="197.32"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:14.26em;">
<span id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Example evaluation problem over <math id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{GF}(11)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#FFFFFF">GF</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathcolor="#FFFFFF" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathcolor="#FFFFFF">11</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathcolor="#FFFFFF" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{GF}(11)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.07 179.11)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:15.19em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:12em;font-size:10pt;" height="175.66" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="210.19"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:15.19em;">
<span id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In a number system where arithmetic on <math id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,\cdots,10\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,\cdots,10\}</annotation></semantics></math> is relabeled as:
<math id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\to\texttt{e0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e0</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\to\texttt{e0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\to\texttt{e1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e1</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\to\texttt{e1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\to\texttt{e9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e9</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\to\texttt{e9}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\to\texttt{e2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e2</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\to\texttt{e2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\to\texttt{e5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e5</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\to\texttt{e5}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\to\texttt{e7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e7</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\to\texttt{e7}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6\to\texttt{e3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e3</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6\to\texttt{e3}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7\to\texttt{e10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">7</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e10</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7\to\texttt{e10}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8\to\texttt{e4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e4</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\to\texttt{e4}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9\to\texttt{e6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e6</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9\to\texttt{e6}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\to\texttt{e8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e8</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\to\texttt{e8}</annotation></semantics></math>.
All addition and multiplication follow modular arithmetic (mod <math id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">I apply these steps to <span id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">e10</span>:</span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Step 1: Add <span id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">e2</span>,</span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Step 2: Add <span id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">e8</span>,</span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Step 3: Multiply by <span id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">e5</span>.</span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p1.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">What is the result?</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="S2.F1.4" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:170.8pt;">
            
<div id="S2.F1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.F1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="238.86" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 236.3 238.86" width="236.3"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,238.86) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 6.37 L 0 232.5 C 0 236.01 2.85 238.86 6.37 238.86 L 229.93 238.86 C 233.45 238.86 236.3 236.01 236.3 232.5 L 236.3 6.37 C 236.3 2.85 233.45 0 229.93 0 L 6.37 0 C 2.85 0 0 2.85 0 6.37 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 6.37 L 0.83 200.96 L 235.47 200.96 L 235.47 6.37 C 235.47 3.31 232.99 0.83 229.93 0.83 L 6.37 0.83 C 3.31 0.83 0.83 3.31 0.83 6.37 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 201.79 L 0.83 232.5 C 0.83 235.55 3.31 238.03 6.37 238.03 L 229.93 238.03 C 232.99 238.03 235.47 235.55 235.47 232.5 L 235.47 201.79 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.07 225.45)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:14.26em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:1.43em;font-size:10pt;" height="28.37" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="197.32"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:14.26em;">
<span id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Example inversion problem over <math id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{GF}(11)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#FFFFFF">GF</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathcolor="#FFFFFF" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathcolor="#FFFFFF">11</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathcolor="#FFFFFF" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{GF}(11)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.07 179.11)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:15.19em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:12em;font-size:10pt;" height="175.66" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="210.19"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:15.19em;">
<span id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In a number system where arithmetic on <math id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,\cdots,10\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,\cdots,10\}</annotation></semantics></math> is relabeled as:
<math id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\to\texttt{e1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e1</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\to\texttt{e1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\to\texttt{e4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e4</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\to\texttt{e4}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\to\texttt{e5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e5</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\to\texttt{e5}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\to\texttt{e8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e8</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\to\texttt{e8}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\to\texttt{e6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e6</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\to\texttt{e6}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\to\texttt{e3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e3</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\to\texttt{e3}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6\to\texttt{e9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e9</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6\to\texttt{e9}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7\to\texttt{e0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">7</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e0</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7\to\texttt{e0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8\to\texttt{e10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e10</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\to\texttt{e10}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9\to\texttt{e2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e2</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9\to\texttt{e2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\to\texttt{e7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e7</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\to\texttt{e7}</annotation></semantics></math>.
All addition and multiplication follow modular arithmetic (mod <math id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">I apply these steps to an unknown element <math id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Step 1: Add <span id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">e8</span>,</span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Step 2: Add <span id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">e4</span>.</span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The result is <span id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">e8</span>.</span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">What is <math id="S2.F1.p2.pic1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>?</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="S2.F1.5" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:170.8pt;">
            
<div id="S2.F1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.F1.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="207.65" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 236.3 207.65" width="236.3"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,207.65) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000066;" fill="#000066" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 6.37 L 0 201.29 C 0 204.8 2.85 207.65 6.37 207.65 L 229.93 207.65 C 233.45 207.65 236.3 204.8 236.3 201.29 L 236.3 6.37 C 236.3 2.85 233.45 0 229.93 0 L 6.37 0 C 2.85 0 0 2.85 0 6.37 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F5F5FF;" fill="#F5F5FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 6.37 L 0.83 170.44 L 235.47 170.44 L 235.47 6.37 C 235.47 3.31 232.99 0.83 229.93 0.83 L 6.37 0.83 C 3.31 0.83 0.83 3.31 0.83 6.37 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000066;" fill="#000066" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 171.27 L 0.83 201.29 C 0.83 204.34 3.31 206.82 6.37 206.82 L 229.93 206.82 C 232.99 206.82 235.47 204.34 235.47 201.29 L 235.47 171.27 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.07 194.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:14.26em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:1.38em;font-size:10pt;" height="27.67" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="197.32"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:14.26em;">
<span id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Forward reasoning on evaluation example</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.07 148.6)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:15.19em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:9.79em;font-size:10pt;" height="145.14" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="210.19"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:15.19em;">
<span id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Read off the inverse mapping: <math id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{e0}=0,\texttt{e1}=1,\texttt{e9}=2,\texttt{e2}=3,\texttt{e5}=4,\texttt{e7}=5,\texttt{e3}=6,\texttt{e10}=7,\texttt{e4}=8,\texttt{e6}=9,\texttt{e8}=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e0</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e1</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e9</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e2</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e5</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e7</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e3</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e10</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">7</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e4</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e6</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e8</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{e0}=0,\texttt{e1}=1,\texttt{e9}=2,\texttt{e2}=3,\texttt{e5}=4,\texttt{e7}=5,\texttt{e3}=6,\texttt{e10}=7,\texttt{e4}=8,\texttt{e6}=9,\texttt{e8}=10</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Start: <math id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{e10}=7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e10</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{e10}=7</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Apply Step 1, Add <math id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{e2}(=3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e2</mtext><mspace style="width:0.389em;" width="0.389em"></mspace><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{e2}(=3)</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7+3\mod 11=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">7</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">mod</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7+3\mod 11=10</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Apply Step 2, Add <math id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{e8}(=10)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e8</mtext><mspace style="width:0.389em;" width="0.389em"></mspace><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{e8}(=10)</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10+10\mod 11=9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">mod</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10+10\mod 11=9</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Apply Step 3, Multiply by <math id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{e5}(=4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e5</mtext><mspace style="width:0.389em;" width="0.389em"></mspace><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{e5}(=4)</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9*4\mod 11=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">mod</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9*4\mod 11=3</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Convert back: <math id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\to\texttt{e2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e2</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\to\texttt{e2}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">#### <span id="S2.F1.p3.pic1.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">e2</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="S2.F1.6" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:170.8pt;">
            
<div id="S2.F1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.F1.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="207.65" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 236.3 207.65" width="236.3"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,207.65) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000066;" fill="#000066" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 6.37 L 0 201.29 C 0 204.8 2.85 207.65 6.37 207.65 L 229.93 207.65 C 233.45 207.65 236.3 204.8 236.3 201.29 L 236.3 6.37 C 236.3 2.85 233.45 0 229.93 0 L 6.37 0 C 2.85 0 0 2.85 0 6.37 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F5F5FF;" fill="#F5F5FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 6.37 L 0.83 170.44 L 235.47 170.44 L 235.47 6.37 C 235.47 3.31 232.99 0.83 229.93 0.83 L 6.37 0.83 C 3.31 0.83 0.83 3.31 0.83 6.37 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000066;" fill="#000066" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 171.27 L 0.83 201.29 C 0.83 204.34 3.31 206.82 6.37 206.82 L 229.93 206.82 C 232.99 206.82 235.47 204.34 235.47 201.29 L 235.47 171.27 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.07 194.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:14.26em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:1.38em;font-size:10pt;" height="27.67" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="197.32"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:14.26em;">
<span id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Forward reasoning on inversion example</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.07 148.6)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:15.19em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:9.79em;font-size:10pt;" height="145.14" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="210.19"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:15.19em;">
<span id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Read off the inverse mapping: <math id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{e1}=0,\texttt{e4}=1,\texttt{e5}=2,\texttt{e8}=3,\texttt{e6}=4,\texttt{e3}=5,\texttt{e9}=6,\texttt{e0}=7,\texttt{e10}=8,\texttt{e2}=9,\texttt{e7}=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e1</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e4</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e5</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e8</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e6</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e3</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e9</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e0</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">7</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e10</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e2</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e7</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{e1}=0,\texttt{e4}=1,\texttt{e5}=2,\texttt{e8}=3,\texttt{e6}=4,\texttt{e3}=5,\texttt{e9}=6,\texttt{e0}=7,\texttt{e10}=8,\texttt{e2}=9,\texttt{e7}=10</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Apply Step 1, Add <math id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{e8}(\texttt{e8}=3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e8</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e8</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{e8}(\texttt{e8}=3)</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+3</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Apply Step 2, Add <math id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{e4}(\texttt{e4}=1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e4</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e4</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{e4}(\texttt{e4}=1)</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+3+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+3+1</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Equation: <math id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1*x+4\equiv 3\pmod{11}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≡</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1*x+4\equiv 3\pmod{11}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1*x\equiv 10\pmod{11}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≡</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1*x\equiv 10\pmod{11}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\equiv 10*1\equiv 10\pmod{11}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≡</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≡</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\equiv 10*1\equiv 10\pmod{11}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Convert back: <math id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\to\texttt{e7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">e7</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\to\texttt{e7}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">#### <span id="S2.F1.p4.pic1.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">e7</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
